# Allow-list for tests/test-prose-pins-are-anchors.sh (issue #1562).
# One `<test-path>:<pattern-prefix>` entry per line, `<test-path>` repo-relative
# (tests/<file>.sh); the entry covers every prose pin in that file whose grep
# pattern starts with <pattern-prefix> (the pattern up to the end of its first
# 5-word run — the lint's UNLISTED line prints it). Blank lines and whole-line
# `#` comments are ignored; every entry block must open with a `#` line saying
# WHY the pin has no token or heading to anchor on.
# Entries only shrink: an entry matching no prose pin fails the lint as STALE.
# See docs/operational-notes.md section 16.

# Legacy CLAUDE.md granularity-contract sentence pin (#459/#492), predates #1562.
